1
00:00:00,709 --> 00:00:04,045
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:10,969 --> 00:00:15,598
<i>As long as I'm in power,</i>
<i>no traitor or rebel</i>

3
00:00:15,682 --> 00:00:17,767
<i>can ever bring the Ardientes down!</i>

4
00:00:17,851 --> 00:00:21,521
[William] <i>That arrogance of theirs</i>
<i>will lead that family to their downfall.</i>

5
00:00:21,604 --> 00:00:23,857
<i>Where are the earnings</i>
<i>from the gambling den?</i>

6
00:00:23,940 --> 00:00:26,025
<i>We have yet to reach</i>
<i>our quota, Congressman.</i>

7
00:00:26,109 --> 00:00:31,781
<i>Just disappear, and don't come back</i>
<i>until I tell you to do so.</i>

8
00:00:31,865 --> 00:00:36,077
<i>Go ahead, Ardientes. Keep belittling me.</i>

9
00:00:36,161 --> 00:00:38,830
<i>I'll drain all your wealth.</i>

10
00:00:39,664 --> 00:00:41,958
[Natalie] <i>Everyone comes back</i>
<i>for a reason.</i>

11
00:00:42,041 --> 00:00:44,878
<i>I still think about how my dad died.</i>

12
00:00:44,961 --> 00:00:50,049
<i>I know someone had him killed,</i>
<i>and I want to know who it is.</i>

13
00:00:50,508 --> 00:00:52,594
<i>-I'll talk. I'm going to talk.</i>
-[Julio] <i>What was that?</i>

14
00:00:52,677 --> 00:00:53,762
<i>I'm going to talk!</i>

15
00:00:53,845 --> 00:00:56,598
<i>-Give me the answer I want.</i>
<i>-The governor.</i>

16
00:00:56,681 --> 00:00:58,224
<i>-Who?</i>
<i>-Alvarez.</i>

17
00:00:58,308 --> 00:01:00,101
[Diego] <i>As long as the Ardientes</i>
<i>are in power,</i>

18
00:01:00,185 --> 00:01:01,186
<i>they can't be brought down.</i>

19
00:01:01,269 --> 00:01:03,188
<i>Someone should fight them head-on.</i>

20
00:01:03,271 --> 00:01:04,731
<i>I'll run for governor.</i>

21
00:01:04,814 --> 00:01:08,735
<i>I will do everything</i>
<i>in my power to help you win.</i>

22
00:01:08,818 --> 00:01:14,365
<i>Sue Governor Alvarez,</i>
<i>and I'll tell you where he is.</i>

23
00:01:14,741 --> 00:01:17,077
[Julio] <i>You are of no use now, Madrigal.</i>

24
00:01:17,160 --> 00:01:18,870
Adios. <i>Go ahead! Do it!</i>

25
00:01:18,953 --> 00:01:19,788
<i>Lower your guns.</i>

26
00:01:19,871 --> 00:01:23,249
<i>We'll use him as a witness</i>
<i>against Alvarez.</i>

27
00:01:23,333 --> 00:01:26,127
<i>Good thing I caught up with you</i>
<i>before you escaped your crimes.</i>

28
00:01:26,211 --> 00:01:28,880
<i>If you're talking about</i>
<i>the spare change I took,</i>

29
00:01:28,963 --> 00:01:31,591
<i>that's nothing compared</i>
<i>to the wealth you all stole.</i>

30
00:01:31,674 --> 00:01:35,011
<i>Alvarez is out, and Emilia is so in!</i>

31
00:01:35,094 --> 00:01:37,472
<i>I, Diego Ardiente-Torillo,</i>

32
00:01:37,555 --> 00:01:41,518
<i>will run as governor of our town</i>
<i>in the next election.</i>

33
00:01:41,601 --> 00:01:44,270
<i>-Go, Diego!</i>
<i>-You'll run for governor?</i>

34
00:01:44,354 --> 00:01:49,484
<i>Once I become governor, I will</i>
<i>be the most powerful Ardiente.</i>

35
00:01:49,567 --> 00:01:53,488
<i>Everyone will bow to the king,</i>
<i>and you will be my queen.</i>

36
00:02:01,121 --> 00:02:02,122
Diego.

37
00:02:03,289 --> 00:02:05,667
Here are the contacts you asked for.

38
00:02:06,292 --> 00:02:09,546
This will help you find
volunteers for your campaign.

39
00:02:10,463 --> 00:02:11,506
Thank you.

40
00:02:12,173 --> 00:02:15,635
You have no idea how thankful
I am to you, Diego.

41
00:02:16,261 --> 00:02:21,057
For helping Lily save Jepoy
from the Ardientes,

42
00:02:21,891 --> 00:02:23,977
despite how close they are to each other.

43
00:02:25,728 --> 00:02:28,648
I know how important Jepoy is to Ivy.

44
00:02:30,066 --> 00:02:32,193
But I'll do everything to help her.

45
00:02:33,403 --> 00:02:39,993
If I could keep her from
ever seeing the Ardientes again,

46
00:02:40,076 --> 00:02:41,244
I would.

47
00:02:42,579 --> 00:02:44,247
I know this is hard for her too.

48
00:02:46,958 --> 00:02:48,501
That goes for me too, Diego.

49
00:02:48,585 --> 00:02:51,421
But if this is how Lily wants to do it…

50
00:02:52,463 --> 00:02:55,550
we have to be there to support her.

51
00:02:56,843 --> 00:03:00,471
And I hope, Diego, you won't let go.

52
00:03:02,432 --> 00:03:05,977
Because Lily's heart
belongs to you and only to you.

53
00:03:09,564 --> 00:03:10,648
I know.

54
00:03:12,191 --> 00:03:14,652
This is just another sacrifice
we have to make.

55
00:03:16,029 --> 00:03:18,531
We have to make
to achieve change in our town.

56
00:03:25,955 --> 00:03:29,918
Um, Papa, it's been days
since the Alvarez fiasco,

57
00:03:30,001 --> 00:03:35,006
and you still haven't appointed
an acting governor.

58
00:03:36,799 --> 00:03:39,636
Don't you think it's about time
you reinstate me?

59
00:03:41,638 --> 00:03:44,515
Everyone thinks you're sick, remember?

60
00:03:44,599 --> 00:03:49,395
Papa, have I still not proven
my capabilities to you?

61
00:03:49,896 --> 00:03:51,648
I will not reinstate you.

62
00:03:52,982 --> 00:03:54,943
There, I've said it. Satisfied?

63
00:03:57,070 --> 00:04:01,532
But, Papa, you have to face
the fact that in no time…

64
00:04:02,242 --> 00:04:06,579
you'll be gone. And as early as now,

65
00:04:06,663 --> 00:04:10,667
I have to be in office
to maintain our family's legacy.

66
00:04:13,503 --> 00:04:14,587
Two things.

67
00:04:14,671 --> 00:04:16,839
First, you're wrong.

68
00:04:18,091 --> 00:04:21,594
You're very wrong because
I am going to live forever.

69
00:04:22,595 --> 00:04:23,763
Secondly,

70
00:04:24,555 --> 00:04:30,103
Arnaldo will run for
governor of Poblacion Ardiente

71
00:04:30,186 --> 00:04:33,064
in the next election, and not you.

72
00:04:34,315 --> 00:04:35,858
Well, that's a good decision

73
00:04:35,942 --> 00:04:38,695
because I don't care
what the feminists say.

74
00:04:39,779 --> 00:04:42,448
Clearly, politics is not
a place for women.

75
00:04:43,366 --> 00:04:46,995
I agree. They all belong in the kitchen.

76
00:04:47,745 --> 00:04:52,375
And between you and Emilia,
I will choose you as governor.

77
00:04:52,917 --> 00:04:56,671
Notwithstanding, of course,
your wrong choices in women.

78
00:04:58,756 --> 00:05:01,634
We're talking about Ivy now. Okay.

79
00:05:03,219 --> 00:05:06,055
I'll prove she's the right choice.

80
00:05:07,223 --> 00:05:09,350
And while I'm at it, I'll also prove

81
00:05:09,434 --> 00:05:14,063
that I will be the best governor
this town could ever have.

82
00:05:18,359 --> 00:05:19,360
Ouch.

83
00:05:25,116 --> 00:05:27,160
[Jepoy] You got everything
you want from me.

84
00:05:27,243 --> 00:05:28,453
I'm no good now.

85
00:05:30,371 --> 00:05:31,497
Let me go!

86
00:05:39,255 --> 00:05:44,927
You can leave this place
if you'll do what I say.

87
00:05:46,012 --> 00:05:49,348
You ratted Alvarez out.

88
00:05:50,475 --> 00:05:51,642
That was the beginning.

89
00:05:51,726 --> 00:05:54,937
Now, you're just going to finish
what you started.

90
00:05:56,189 --> 00:05:59,650
It's simple. Another's head
in exchange for yours, Madrigal.

91
00:06:02,070 --> 00:06:04,697
Bring me Alvarez's head…

92
00:06:07,325 --> 00:06:08,659
and I'll set you free.

93
00:06:10,620 --> 00:06:12,163
I won't do what you want.

94
00:06:14,624 --> 00:06:18,211
Well, then. I'll be outside, just in case.

95
00:06:19,587 --> 00:06:23,925
Now, if you're ready to talk to me,

96
00:06:24,008 --> 00:06:27,220
you can tell any of my men here.

97
00:06:27,845 --> 00:06:29,722
Just don't think of running away.

98
00:06:30,973 --> 00:06:34,227
Because my men won't hesitate to kill you.

99
00:06:36,187 --> 00:06:37,939
I'm not afraid to die.

100
00:06:38,356 --> 00:06:40,108
[chuckles]

101
00:06:42,485 --> 00:06:44,695
You can't fool me.

102
00:06:46,114 --> 00:06:48,157
Everybody's afraid to die.

103
00:06:49,283 --> 00:06:51,911
You most of all.

104
00:06:53,454 --> 00:06:56,999
You, who went through so much trouble.

105
00:06:57,625 --> 00:07:02,797
You gave me Alvarez just so
I wouldn't kill you.

106
00:07:03,965 --> 00:07:08,803
You value your life too much,
more than anything else.

107
00:07:08,886 --> 00:07:11,055
Oh, and there's one more thing
that you value.

108
00:07:14,016 --> 00:07:15,726
Your freedom.

109
00:07:16,894 --> 00:07:19,439
Now, you will kill Alvarez…

110
00:07:21,983 --> 00:07:25,820
in exchange for your life and freedom.

111
00:07:26,237 --> 00:07:28,489
[ominous music playing]

112
00:07:33,161 --> 00:07:34,787
Hurry! Get that out of here!

113
00:07:35,913 --> 00:07:38,708
This one too. That one.

114
00:07:38,791 --> 00:07:42,295
That belongs to the police
blotter and not in this office!

115
00:07:44,172 --> 00:07:45,173
Hurry!

116
00:07:47,633 --> 00:07:50,678
Are you sure Julio isn't going
to mind what you're doing?

117
00:07:51,679 --> 00:07:53,264
Of course not, Aunt Claire.

118
00:07:54,307 --> 00:07:58,936
I'll inch my way back to this
position by hook or by crook.

119
00:07:59,854 --> 00:08:05,193
Because I am preparing
my comeback as the queen.

120
00:08:08,070 --> 00:08:09,197
The queen?

121
00:08:10,364 --> 00:08:12,992
My dear, there's going to be a new king.

122
00:08:13,659 --> 00:08:17,413
And I'm pretty sure
he will have his own queen.

123
00:08:19,790 --> 00:08:22,168
Emilia, you're slowly being eased out.

124
00:08:22,793 --> 00:08:23,920
[line ringing]

125
00:08:24,712 --> 00:08:26,005
Hello, Martinez?

126
00:08:27,006 --> 00:08:29,008
Talk to the private investigator,

127
00:08:29,091 --> 00:08:32,303
and find out more about Ivy Aguas.

128
00:08:35,181 --> 00:08:37,475
I will not be pushed
to the sidelines, Auntie.

129
00:08:37,558 --> 00:08:40,853
Especially once I prove to my family

130
00:08:40,937 --> 00:08:45,525
that Ivy Aguas is connected
to Camia Cruz and Madrigal.

131
00:08:45,900 --> 00:08:50,154
And when that happens,
I'll be the hero of the family.

132
00:08:53,991 --> 00:08:55,910
Oh. How I miss this chair.

133
00:08:58,663 --> 00:08:59,747
[chuckles]

134
00:09:02,708 --> 00:09:04,544
[ominous music playing]

135
00:09:06,254 --> 00:09:08,214
And what if I refuse again?

136
00:09:11,551 --> 00:09:16,222
I have my men watching your every move.

137
00:09:16,722 --> 00:09:19,850
They know every decision you make.

138
00:09:21,018 --> 00:09:27,900
And if you change your mind
and think of escaping…

139
00:09:28,776 --> 00:09:32,738
or even if you go slightly off-target…

140
00:09:33,364 --> 00:09:38,869
I have snipers ready
to blow your brains out.

141
00:09:40,621 --> 00:09:44,542
But then again, I'm sure you
wouldn't want that, would you?

142
00:09:44,959 --> 00:09:46,419
I wouldn't want to do that.

143
00:09:49,338 --> 00:09:50,381
Well?

144
00:09:54,010 --> 00:09:55,011
Hmm.

145
00:09:56,679 --> 00:09:59,056
Silence means yes.

146
00:10:01,892 --> 00:10:03,227
Good boy.

147
00:10:04,562 --> 00:10:08,608
Good boy, Madrigal. Go and get him.

148
00:10:09,609 --> 00:10:10,860
And, please…

149
00:10:12,403 --> 00:10:13,904
don't disappoint me.

150
00:10:16,407 --> 00:10:17,325
[elevator chimes]

151
00:10:17,992 --> 00:10:20,411
[ominous music playing]

152
00:10:21,996 --> 00:10:23,164
[phone ringing]

153
00:10:26,417 --> 00:10:27,460
Hello?

154
00:10:28,502 --> 00:10:29,795
Yeah? Where's the chopper?

155
00:10:38,387 --> 00:10:40,848
What's taking you so long?
I've been waiting here. Hurry!

156
00:10:45,102 --> 00:10:46,687
[doorbell chimes]

157
00:10:46,771 --> 00:10:47,813
Hold on.

158
00:11:03,454 --> 00:11:05,831
[tense music playing]

159
00:11:14,006 --> 00:11:15,007
[grunts]

160
00:11:15,674 --> 00:11:16,675
[groans]

161
00:11:18,302 --> 00:11:19,220
[thuds]

162
00:11:27,478 --> 00:11:28,521
[grunts]

163
00:11:33,234 --> 00:11:35,653
[tense music playing]

164
00:11:38,197 --> 00:11:39,198
[groans]

165
00:11:51,252 --> 00:11:53,379
[tense music playing]

166
00:11:59,260 --> 00:12:00,302
Alvarez!

167
00:12:03,013 --> 00:12:04,098
Stay away from me!

168
00:12:05,099 --> 00:12:06,684
I know Julio sent you.

169
00:12:07,268 --> 00:12:08,477
Don't come any closer!

170
00:12:10,479 --> 00:12:13,023
Don't let the Ardientes
control you, Madrigal.

171
00:12:14,483 --> 00:12:16,026
You don't have to do this.

172
00:12:20,406 --> 00:12:21,323
[grunts]

173
00:12:22,992 --> 00:12:23,868
[groans]

174
00:12:28,038 --> 00:12:28,998
[grunts]

175
00:12:38,299 --> 00:12:40,926
[grunting]

176
00:12:55,232 --> 00:12:56,358
[screams]

177
00:12:58,611 --> 00:12:59,612
[thuds]

178
00:13:05,576 --> 00:13:07,119
[ominous music playing]

179
00:13:20,799 --> 00:13:23,552
[ominous music playing]

180
00:13:29,767 --> 00:13:32,228
<i>Governor William Alvarez was found dead</i>

181
00:13:32,311 --> 00:13:34,522
<i>at the Pacific Winds Hotel.</i>

182
00:13:34,605 --> 00:13:36,065
<i>According to multiple witness statements,</i>

183
00:13:36,148 --> 00:13:38,442
<i>there's a possibility of foul play.</i>

184
00:13:39,151 --> 00:13:40,569
<i>Let's interview one of the witnesses.</i>

185
00:13:40,653 --> 00:13:44,198
[woman] <i>I saw the governor with</i>
<i>a man on the hotel rooftop.</i>

186
00:13:44,281 --> 00:13:48,285
<i>He was wearing a cap</i>
<i>and looked pretty tall.</i>

187
00:13:48,369 --> 00:13:50,538
<i>It looked like he</i>
<i>and the governor were fighting.</i>

188
00:13:50,621 --> 00:13:52,873
<i>Then, I saw the governor</i>
<i>jump down from the building.</i>

189
00:13:55,876 --> 00:13:56,752
It's Jepoy.

190
00:13:57,378 --> 00:13:59,255
I'm sure they're referring to him.

191
00:14:00,089 --> 00:14:01,674
Those wretched Ardientes!

192
00:14:02,341 --> 00:14:04,927
They forced Jepoy
to kill Governor Alvarez.

193
00:14:05,803 --> 00:14:07,054
They're monsters!

194
00:14:08,389 --> 00:14:12,393
But, Lily, if Jepoy was ordered
to kill Alvarez,

195
00:14:12,476 --> 00:14:14,562
the Ardientes might set him free now.

196
00:14:15,771 --> 00:14:18,399
[clapping]

197
00:14:20,359 --> 00:14:23,529
Job well done, Madrigal!

198
00:14:24,989 --> 00:14:27,074
Come here. Join me.

199
00:14:27,616 --> 00:14:29,869
Drink with me. Drink with me.

200
00:14:32,788 --> 00:14:33,831
Okay.

201
00:14:36,417 --> 00:14:39,003
This is yours. Okay?

202
00:14:40,379 --> 00:14:41,547
To your health!

203
00:14:48,345 --> 00:14:52,474
I don't need that. We had an agreement.

204
00:14:53,100 --> 00:14:56,979
You said you'd set me free.
Let me go! Let me go now!

205
00:14:59,481 --> 00:15:01,984
[clicks tongue]

206
00:15:03,777 --> 00:15:05,195
What's the rush?

207
00:15:06,196 --> 00:15:07,197
Cheers.

208
00:15:07,865 --> 00:15:11,327
For your freedom,

209
00:15:12,453 --> 00:15:16,582
and for your nearing encounter
with the devil or Grim Reaper,

210
00:15:16,665 --> 00:15:17,833
whoever comes first.

211
00:15:19,543 --> 00:15:22,087
No. You don't know the Ardientes.

212
00:15:22,796 --> 00:15:28,052
They're all cunning…
Grandpa, Mom, and Arnaldo.

213
00:15:28,135 --> 00:15:29,386
What are you trying to say?

214
00:15:30,846 --> 00:15:34,892
They might let Jepoy live
as long as he's useful to them.

215
00:15:35,392 --> 00:15:38,270
-And if he isn't?
-They'll kill him.

216
00:15:39,897 --> 00:15:41,899
You know, I don't need you anymore.

217
00:15:42,775 --> 00:15:45,778
You are useless.

218
00:15:47,112 --> 00:15:49,990
I can give you the freedom you want,

219
00:15:50,074 --> 00:15:52,826
but let's play a game first.

220
00:15:55,621 --> 00:15:59,667
We're now going to play a game
called Russian roulette.

221
00:16:01,710 --> 00:16:02,753
One bullet.

222
00:16:04,964 --> 00:16:06,548
Six chambers.

223
00:16:10,678 --> 00:16:12,221
This is how the game goes.

224
00:16:12,554 --> 00:16:15,307
I'll spin the gun's cylinder,

225
00:16:16,183 --> 00:16:18,811
and then aim it at your forehead.

226
00:16:20,104 --> 00:16:21,689
If I pull the trigger and it fires…

227
00:16:23,190 --> 00:16:24,358
I'm sorry, you're dead.

228
00:16:25,150 --> 00:16:28,195
If not, we'll do it over again.

229
00:16:29,446 --> 00:16:30,239
Watch.

230
00:16:32,741 --> 00:16:33,742
Okay.

231
00:16:36,662 --> 00:16:37,913
No! Don't! No!

232
00:16:38,872 --> 00:16:39,957
[groans]

233
00:16:40,040 --> 00:16:45,004
As I said, I know you value your
life more than anything else.

234
00:16:45,713 --> 00:16:46,839
Ready?

235
00:16:48,549 --> 00:16:50,676
Hmm? Any last words?

236
00:16:51,468 --> 00:16:52,469
-Huh?!
-[gun clicks]

237
00:16:52,928 --> 00:16:55,305
-You bastard!
-[laughs]

238
00:16:55,806 --> 00:16:57,558
You evil bastard! You lied to me!

239
00:16:58,934 --> 00:17:00,769
You don't keep your word, you bastard!

240
00:17:01,603 --> 00:17:03,647
That's enough. Enough!

241
00:17:03,731 --> 00:17:05,858
-Honestly, Madrigal.
-You're insane!

242
00:17:05,941 --> 00:17:08,652
Do you think I'm a fool?
Do you think I'm insane?

243
00:17:09,194 --> 00:17:10,362
I tell you what, Madrigal.

244
00:17:10,988 --> 00:17:14,783
I have full control of my faculties.

245
00:17:16,076 --> 00:17:20,372
It's just that I love playing this game!

246
00:17:21,832 --> 00:17:23,459
[laughs]

247
00:17:24,460 --> 00:17:25,461
Hey!

248
00:17:25,794 --> 00:17:27,671
Get him out of here. I'm tired.

249
00:17:27,755 --> 00:17:29,089
-Let's go!
-[grunts]

250
00:17:29,923 --> 00:17:31,550
[Julio] I'm sick and tired of this game.

251
00:17:32,259 --> 00:17:34,720
[laughing]

252
00:17:36,680 --> 00:17:40,976
I'm not crazy, Madrigal. I'm not crazy.

253
00:17:42,186 --> 00:17:44,188
I won't allow that to happen to Jepoy.

254
00:17:45,397 --> 00:17:46,982
Wait. Where are you going?

255
00:17:48,025 --> 00:17:50,944
I'll go to the Ardientes
and save my friend.

256
00:17:53,197 --> 00:17:54,865
You can't leave.

257
00:17:54,948 --> 00:17:56,075
You can't stop me.

258
00:17:56,158 --> 00:17:57,659
I need to save Jepoy. Get out of my way.

259
00:17:57,743 --> 00:17:59,078
-No. I won't.
-What's wrong with you?

260
00:17:59,161 --> 00:18:01,163
I'll do it! I'll save him. Not you.

261
00:18:01,246 --> 00:18:02,498
You are not going to do that.

262
00:18:02,581 --> 00:18:04,291
I'm his friend, so I'll be
the one to save Jepoy.

263
00:18:04,374 --> 00:18:05,959
-I know. He's your friend.
-Diego!

264
00:18:06,043 --> 00:18:07,503
-Listen to me!
-Diego, stop!

265
00:18:07,586 --> 00:18:10,214
Yes, he's your friend, but I love you!

266
00:18:12,299 --> 00:18:14,218
If you get caught, you're done for.

267
00:18:14,635 --> 00:18:16,929
It will be the end of you and our fight.

268
00:18:17,012 --> 00:18:19,848
But I'll die first before that happens.

269
00:18:23,519 --> 00:18:25,646
Ivy, I won't allow you
to put yourself in danger.

270
00:18:26,605 --> 00:18:27,606
Ivy.

271
00:18:28,190 --> 00:18:31,902
Ivy, trust me. I'll get Jepoy back.

272
00:18:31,985 --> 00:18:33,987
I'll bring him back safe and sound.

273
00:18:36,156 --> 00:18:37,282
I promise.

274
00:18:41,370 --> 00:18:43,497
Here. Fix yourself up.

275
00:18:44,206 --> 00:18:46,416
So you'll look presentable
when you're six feet under.

276
00:18:54,424 --> 00:18:57,219
[ominous music playing]

277
00:19:22,619 --> 00:19:24,663
[ominous music playing]

278
00:19:47,436 --> 00:19:49,938
[ominous music playing]

279
00:20:17,007 --> 00:20:19,301
<i>I'll do everything to protect you.</i>

280
00:20:22,095 --> 00:20:23,680
<i>Until my last breath.</i>

281
00:20:39,363 --> 00:20:42,074
[ominous music playing]

282
00:20:59,424 --> 00:21:02,052
[ominous music playing]

283
00:21:16,942 --> 00:21:19,569
[huffing]

284
00:21:30,998 --> 00:21:33,792
Ivy, Jepoy already
accomplished his mission.

285
00:21:35,085 --> 00:21:37,254
Why hasn't he come back yet?

286
00:21:38,588 --> 00:21:41,008
Why does Julio still have him?

287
00:21:41,883 --> 00:21:47,055
If I could just ask Congressman
to let go of Jepoy,

288
00:21:47,139 --> 00:21:49,016
I'll do it, Ivy.

289
00:21:49,683 --> 00:21:53,687
No, Nanny. You can't do that.

290
00:21:53,770 --> 00:21:57,232
I don't want you
to put yourself in danger.

291
00:21:59,943 --> 00:22:02,404
I'm worried about Jepoy too.

292
00:22:04,072 --> 00:22:09,411
But Diego promised me
that he would save him.

293
00:22:11,997 --> 00:22:13,248
All right, Ivy.

294
00:22:19,296 --> 00:22:21,840
Can you believe that?
Governor Alvarez is dead.

295
00:22:21,923 --> 00:22:23,800
I know. Anyway, I'll go charge my phone.

296
00:22:23,884 --> 00:22:24,968
-Sure.
-Okay.

297
00:22:25,052 --> 00:22:26,219
But hurry up, I'll be alone here.

298
00:22:26,303 --> 00:22:27,471
Okay. Sure, sure.

299
00:22:34,186 --> 00:22:35,187
[groans]

300
00:22:37,147 --> 00:22:38,148
[groans]

301
00:22:44,905 --> 00:22:45,906
[thuds]

302
00:22:53,246 --> 00:22:54,289
[groans]

303
00:23:01,213 --> 00:23:03,840
[tense music playing]

304
00:23:27,739 --> 00:23:29,950
[tense music playing]

305
00:23:37,290 --> 00:23:38,708
[grunts]

306
00:23:42,879 --> 00:23:44,172
[metal clanking]

307
00:23:44,881 --> 00:23:49,177
Jepoy! Jepoy. It's me, Diego!
Jepoy, it's me!

308
00:23:52,973 --> 00:23:53,890
[grunts]

309
00:23:58,562 --> 00:23:59,563
[clattering]

310
00:24:03,733 --> 00:24:04,734
[grunts]

311
00:24:08,405 --> 00:24:09,406
Jepoy, I'm Diego!

312
00:24:10,782 --> 00:24:11,825
It's Diego!

313
00:24:13,952 --> 00:24:15,662
[grunting]

314
00:24:20,876 --> 00:24:24,588
No, don't! Don't take it off,
there are cameras!

315
00:24:24,671 --> 00:24:25,755
There are cameras here.

316
00:24:25,839 --> 00:24:27,424
-Jepoy--
-What are you doing here?

317
00:24:27,507 --> 00:24:29,134
Jepoy, I'm busting you out of here.

318
00:24:31,052 --> 00:24:32,554
We're going to escape.

319
00:24:34,806 --> 00:24:35,807
Jepoy!

320
00:24:36,516 --> 00:24:39,227
[gunshots]

321
00:24:42,731 --> 00:24:44,941
[gunshots]

322
00:24:52,324 --> 00:24:53,617
[clattering]

323
00:25:05,337 --> 00:25:06,671
[grunting]

324
00:25:08,256 --> 00:25:09,257
[clinks]

325
00:25:23,271 --> 00:25:24,272
Let's go!

326
00:25:33,949 --> 00:25:36,284
-Jepoy! Jepoy! Mom!
-Ivy.

327
00:25:36,368 --> 00:25:37,702
-Jepoy!
-Jepoy!

328
00:25:37,786 --> 00:25:39,329
Here. Bring him here.

329
00:25:40,622 --> 00:25:41,623
Jepoy!

330
00:25:42,499 --> 00:25:44,376
-Jepoy! Jepoy!
-Jepoy!

331
00:25:44,459 --> 00:25:46,878
You're back! You're back home!

332
00:25:46,962 --> 00:25:49,923
What happened? What did they do to you?

333
00:25:50,006 --> 00:25:51,591
I'm glad you're all right!

334
00:25:51,675 --> 00:25:53,468
Jepoy, what happened to you?

335
00:25:55,637 --> 00:25:57,430
Ivy, Diego's been shot!

336
00:25:57,514 --> 00:25:58,556
Diego!

337
00:25:59,766 --> 00:26:00,725
Guards!

338
00:26:00,809 --> 00:26:03,478
Diego, what happened? Guards, help me!

339
00:26:03,561 --> 00:26:04,646
Diego!

340
00:26:04,729 --> 00:26:05,814
Guards, here.

341
00:26:06,648 --> 00:26:07,816
Quick!

342
00:26:07,899 --> 00:26:10,110
Mom! Nanny! I need a towel.

343
00:26:10,193 --> 00:26:12,153
-Carlotta!
-Get me water, quick!

344
00:26:12,237 --> 00:26:13,405
Diego, what happened?

345
00:26:16,199 --> 00:26:18,159
-Auntie.
-Here it is, dear.

346
00:26:18,660 --> 00:26:20,328
Mom, I need to remove the bullet.

347
00:26:22,330 --> 00:26:23,331
[groans]

348
00:26:24,207 --> 00:26:26,334
Diego. Diego. Diego.

349
00:26:26,418 --> 00:26:29,254
Nanny, please call a doctor! Please!

350
00:26:29,838 --> 00:26:31,214
-[Diego grunts]
-[Ivy] Diego.

351
00:26:43,310 --> 00:26:45,020
I've sent the doctor home.

352
00:26:45,103 --> 00:26:50,150
Jepoy, I've arranged for you
to stay at the rest house.

353
00:26:50,984 --> 00:26:52,360
That won't be necessary, Ivy.

354
00:26:53,028 --> 00:26:54,362
What do you mean?

355
00:26:54,946 --> 00:26:57,532
Jepoy, I'm sure the Ardientes
are looking for you.

356
00:26:57,615 --> 00:26:59,993
-You have to hide.
-I know that.

357
00:27:00,493 --> 00:27:01,870
You're right, I need to hide.

358
00:27:04,581 --> 00:27:06,249
But not at your rest house.

359
00:27:07,959 --> 00:27:09,044
I can't stay there.

360
00:27:10,211 --> 00:27:13,006
Jepoy, what do you mean?

361
00:27:13,506 --> 00:27:14,799
As long as I'm connected with Ivy,

362
00:27:14,883 --> 00:27:17,344
the Ardientes will continue
to be suspicious of her.

363
00:27:23,183 --> 00:27:24,642
Ivy, I'm the key.

364
00:27:26,644 --> 00:27:28,396
I'm the time bomb
they're waiting on to explode

365
00:27:28,480 --> 00:27:29,981
so they'll find out who you really are.

366
00:27:30,065 --> 00:27:31,900
If you hide me in your rest house…

367
00:27:32,525 --> 00:27:35,403
the danger of them discovering
your real plans will persist.

368
00:27:37,238 --> 00:27:37,989
Jepoy…

369
00:27:38,073 --> 00:27:40,909
Ivy, they'll find out you're Lily.

370
00:27:50,627 --> 00:27:52,670
I have to cut ties with you.

371
00:27:54,089 --> 00:27:55,882
I have to go away.

372
00:28:07,477 --> 00:28:09,187
I have to stay away from you, Ivy.

373
00:28:21,574 --> 00:28:23,701
[slow instrumental playing]

374
00:28:53,189 --> 00:28:57,652
If not for you, something worse
might've happened to Jepoy.

375
00:29:02,490 --> 00:29:03,992
He's important to you.

376
00:29:05,410 --> 00:29:06,661
So I helped him escape.

377
00:29:17,881 --> 00:29:19,299
Ivy, I'll do everything…

378
00:29:21,384 --> 00:29:23,678
everything to make
you happy because I love you.

379
00:29:26,514 --> 00:29:28,057
Even if you love me or not…

380
00:29:30,226 --> 00:29:32,979
my feelings for you will never change.

381
00:29:38,026 --> 00:29:39,152
No matter what.

382
00:29:43,907 --> 00:29:45,575
This isn't the right time, Diego.

383
00:29:49,245 --> 00:29:50,246
I know.

384
00:29:54,751 --> 00:29:55,919
I'll wait for you.

385
00:30:04,093 --> 00:30:06,304
[slow instrumental playing]

386
00:30:13,520 --> 00:30:16,773
[Jepoy] <i>Ivy, my time is running out.</i>

387
00:30:18,733 --> 00:30:20,902
<i>Julio Ardiente will kill me.</i>

388
00:30:22,862 --> 00:30:25,114
<i>If not now, maybe tomorrow.</i>

389
00:30:30,203 --> 00:30:31,996
[Jepoy] May I have some coffee?

390
00:30:32,080 --> 00:30:33,331
[woman] Be right there.

391
00:30:36,209 --> 00:30:37,919
[Jepoy] <i>I need to stay away from you.</i>

392
00:30:40,129 --> 00:30:42,382
<i>As long as the Ardientes are after me…</i>

393
00:30:43,132 --> 00:30:48,221
<i>there's the threat of them</i>
<i>discovering that you are Lily.</i>

394
00:30:49,764 --> 00:30:51,140
[police officer]
Are you done preparing this?

395
00:30:51,224 --> 00:30:52,308
I'll get it now, okay?

396
00:30:53,101 --> 00:30:54,811
-Okay.
-Here you go.

397
00:31:02,944 --> 00:31:04,320
[Jepoy] <i>Even if I'm not with you…</i>

398
00:31:05,446 --> 00:31:07,991
<i>I know that Diego is there for you.</i>

399
00:31:10,577 --> 00:31:13,496
<i>He'll love you like I love you.</i>

400
00:31:14,706 --> 00:31:15,957
<i>Maybe even more.</i>

401
00:31:20,420 --> 00:31:23,590
<i>Yours, Jepoy.</i>

402
00:31:49,198 --> 00:31:51,743
I'm supposed to give
a commemorative speech

403
00:31:51,826 --> 00:31:54,203
for the death of Alvarez.

404
00:31:55,538 --> 00:31:57,624
But why would I honor that traitor?

405
00:32:00,084 --> 00:32:01,127
I understand.

406
00:32:02,962 --> 00:32:05,298
But the way I see it…

407
00:32:06,299 --> 00:32:09,636
I can use the venue
to announce my candidacy.

408
00:32:11,888 --> 00:32:13,348
Good thinking!

409
00:32:14,307 --> 00:32:16,726
Let's not waste that opportunity, then.

410
00:32:17,685 --> 00:32:21,439
And let's do this to reinforce the fact…

411
00:32:22,982 --> 00:32:29,322
that no one can go against the Ardientes.

412
00:32:29,822 --> 00:32:31,199
[knocks on door]

413
00:32:33,117 --> 00:32:33,993
[Julio] Hey!

414
00:32:34,077 --> 00:32:37,330
Who said you could barge in like that?!

415
00:32:37,413 --> 00:32:39,707
I'm sorry, Congressman.
But Madrigal escaped.

416
00:32:40,750 --> 00:32:41,751
Darn it!

417
00:32:49,133 --> 00:32:52,303
Jepoy left without even saying
goodbye to me.

418
00:32:52,679 --> 00:32:55,139
We didn't get the chance to talk, Ivy.

419
00:32:56,432 --> 00:32:57,558
Nanny.

420
00:32:57,642 --> 00:32:59,811
I didn't say goodbye.

421
00:33:00,395 --> 00:33:01,479
Carlotta.

422
00:33:02,230 --> 00:33:06,234
Camia, I treated Jepoy like my own.

423
00:33:07,235 --> 00:33:10,405
What if he gets in trouble? What if…

424
00:33:11,531 --> 00:33:14,575
What if they find him, Ivy?

425
00:33:14,659 --> 00:33:17,745
The Ardientes will kill him!

426
00:33:19,497 --> 00:33:22,333
I know where you're coming from.

427
00:33:24,502 --> 00:33:28,798
But he decided this on his own.
He has his reasons.

428
00:33:30,675 --> 00:33:32,552
We both know Jepoy.

429
00:33:33,469 --> 00:33:34,929
He can take care of himself.

430
00:33:36,806 --> 00:33:38,766
Diego's right, Carlotta.

431
00:33:39,183 --> 00:33:42,311
It'll be hard for me
to respect his decision.

432
00:33:44,272 --> 00:33:48,943
But I'm certain he did that
for Ivy's safety.

433
00:33:58,536 --> 00:34:01,456
[Julio screaming]

434
00:34:03,624 --> 00:34:06,335
Idiots! Morons!

435
00:34:07,503 --> 00:34:10,548
You bunch of imbeciles!

436
00:34:11,591 --> 00:34:17,096
Can one of you explain to me

437
00:34:17,180 --> 00:34:22,727
how exactly someone tortured to near death

438
00:34:22,810 --> 00:34:24,437
managed to escape you?!

439
00:34:24,979 --> 00:34:28,983
You have eyes, don't you?! You have feet!

440
00:34:29,984 --> 00:34:32,445
Your problem is, you don't have brains!

441
00:34:32,528 --> 00:34:33,571
[gunshot]

442
00:34:35,656 --> 00:34:38,409
Papa, I think Ivy Aguas
had something to do with this.

443
00:34:38,493 --> 00:34:41,037
Can you please stop
dragging Ivy into this mess?

444
00:34:41,120 --> 00:34:42,580
Arnaldo, I have proof

445
00:34:42,663 --> 00:34:45,583
that Madrigal and Ivy are accomplices.

446
00:34:45,666 --> 00:34:47,418
Shut up, Emilia.

447
00:34:49,670 --> 00:34:52,548
You, Domingo.

448
00:34:53,341 --> 00:34:57,678
Did you see who helped Madrigal escape?

449
00:34:58,554 --> 00:35:02,183
No, Congressman. He was wearing a mask.

450
00:35:02,683 --> 00:35:04,227
But we're sure it was a guy.

451
00:35:06,187 --> 00:35:08,272
You're sure it was a guy?

452
00:35:08,606 --> 00:35:09,607
[gunshot]

453
00:35:16,864 --> 00:35:17,865
Miss Carlotta…

454
00:35:18,950 --> 00:35:20,535
Ivy, I have to go.

455
00:35:20,618 --> 00:35:21,661
Okay, Diego.

456
00:35:22,078 --> 00:35:23,037
Diego…

457
00:35:24,789 --> 00:35:29,502
Thank you so much.
Thank you for saving Jepoy.

458
00:35:31,504 --> 00:35:32,630
I'll be upstairs.

459
00:35:34,090 --> 00:35:35,633
I'll be there in a bit.

460
00:35:40,513 --> 00:35:43,224
I told you I'd do anything for you.

461
00:35:44,016 --> 00:35:45,935
For the people important to you.

462
00:35:49,272 --> 00:35:50,606
You should get some rest.

463
00:35:51,899 --> 00:35:54,610
I hope you'll feel a little
better tomorrow morning.

464
00:35:58,781 --> 00:36:00,449
This will last the whole night.

465
00:36:02,785 --> 00:36:05,121
But tomorrow, we fight again.

466
00:36:08,207 --> 00:36:09,250
Take care.

467
00:36:13,504 --> 00:36:14,589
Ivy, wait.

468
00:36:18,301 --> 00:36:20,928
I hope you don't take this
the wrong way but…

469
00:36:23,097 --> 00:36:24,807
Is it okay if I sleep here?

470
00:36:28,144 --> 00:36:29,145
Why?

471
00:36:32,398 --> 00:36:33,941
I want to protect you.

472
00:36:54,754 --> 00:36:55,922
[knocks on door]

473
00:36:57,423 --> 00:36:58,424
Diego--

474
00:37:08,643 --> 00:37:09,644
Uh…

475
00:37:13,773 --> 00:37:16,609
I brought you some extra sheets.

476
00:37:20,279 --> 00:37:21,322
Thanks.

477
00:37:24,283 --> 00:37:26,369
It's a good thing you're here.

478
00:37:28,955 --> 00:37:33,709
Because to be honest,
I'm still worried for you.

479
00:37:35,503 --> 00:37:38,464
I'm glad you're here
so we can protect each other.

480
00:37:40,383 --> 00:37:43,052
I can't imagine what will happen when…

481
00:37:44,679 --> 00:37:48,432
you're face-to-face with the Ardientes,

482
00:37:48,516 --> 00:37:52,311
especially when you run for governor.

483
00:37:53,229 --> 00:37:54,981
You're worried about me?

484
00:37:56,774 --> 00:38:00,987
You're like a lamb in a cage of lions
when you're with the Ardientes.

485
00:38:01,737 --> 00:38:05,866
What if they discover your plans
and find out who you really are?

486
00:38:05,950 --> 00:38:07,868
I'm only human, Diego.

487
00:38:09,537 --> 00:38:12,832
I get hurt and angry.

488
00:38:14,375 --> 00:38:16,877
When I'm with the Ardientes,

489
00:38:17,586 --> 00:38:20,756
I can't help but loathe them more.

490
00:38:22,341 --> 00:38:28,264
But I need to do this,
to pretend, to befriend them…

491
00:38:30,141 --> 00:38:32,018
so I can bring them down.

492
00:38:36,397 --> 00:38:37,398
Ivy…

493
00:38:43,321 --> 00:38:49,118
We can live a simple life.
Why do we have to do this?

494
00:38:50,036 --> 00:38:52,955
I can't afford a simple life, Diego.

495
00:38:54,248 --> 00:38:57,418
Because I won't be able to forgive myself

496
00:38:57,501 --> 00:39:00,963
if I don't do anything
about the Ardientes.

497
00:39:03,049 --> 00:39:06,385
If they don't pay for what they've done.

498
00:39:11,098 --> 00:39:12,516
Go on, get some rest.

499
00:39:13,225 --> 00:39:14,352
Ivy…

500
00:39:14,435 --> 00:39:17,355
["Sa'Yo" instrumental playing]

501
00:39:22,276 --> 00:39:23,986
Ivy, I promise you…

502
00:39:25,196 --> 00:39:30,284
that I'll be here to fight
for you no matter what.

503
00:39:39,377 --> 00:39:42,171
["Sa'Yo" by Silent Sanctuary playing]

504
00:40:05,653 --> 00:40:07,071
[phone ringing]

505
00:40:11,742 --> 00:40:13,119
Yes, Mr. Mayor?

506
00:40:17,998 --> 00:40:19,041
Mr. Mayor?

507
00:40:19,792 --> 00:40:21,961
Mr. Mayor, I came as soon as I heard.

508
00:40:22,670 --> 00:40:24,046
-Sit down.
-I can't believe it.

509
00:40:24,130 --> 00:40:27,049
How'd Madrigal manage to escape?

510
00:40:27,425 --> 00:40:30,678
Maybe because he had
an accomplice within our circle?

511
00:40:31,303 --> 00:40:32,304
No, Mom.

512
00:40:32,388 --> 00:40:34,515
The guards said somebody rescued him.

513
00:40:35,307 --> 00:40:36,308
But there's no need to worry.

514
00:40:36,392 --> 00:40:39,145
Our men are looking for him
and his accomplice.

515
00:40:39,854 --> 00:40:42,857
That's why we had to push back
the commemoration

516
00:40:42,940 --> 00:40:45,443
and the program at the town hall.

517
00:40:45,985 --> 00:40:47,695
Because we have to devote all our time

518
00:40:47,778 --> 00:40:49,864
to catch Madrigal right away.

519
00:40:53,075 --> 00:40:56,620
Congressman, isn't it more
important to push through

520
00:40:56,704 --> 00:41:00,624
with the public address
instead of looking for Madrigal?

521
00:41:01,417 --> 00:41:04,211
Why don't you use the event tomorrow

522
00:41:04,295 --> 00:41:06,672
to spread the word
about the search for Madrigal?

523
00:41:07,339 --> 00:41:10,009
[Arnaldo] Why not?
I think she has a point.

524
00:41:10,092 --> 00:41:12,595
Why don't we follow the original schedule,

525
00:41:12,678 --> 00:41:15,723
and then let's instruct our men

526
00:41:15,806 --> 00:41:18,267
to initiate a full-blown manhunt
for Madrigal.

527
00:41:20,060 --> 00:41:21,103
What do you think, Grandpa?

528
00:41:23,063 --> 00:41:24,064
[Ivy sighs]

529
00:41:24,398 --> 00:41:28,611
How did Madrigal even escape?
And who helped him?

530
00:41:35,451 --> 00:41:36,494
[Martinez] Ma'am.

531
00:41:36,869 --> 00:41:37,995
Ma'am.

532
00:41:38,704 --> 00:41:40,706
My goodness, Martinez. Out of nowhere.

533
00:41:40,789 --> 00:41:42,416
You're going to give me a heart attack.

534
00:41:42,500 --> 00:41:44,043
Ma'am, I have the files you asked for

535
00:41:44,126 --> 00:41:45,628
from your private investigator.

536
00:41:47,671 --> 00:41:48,714
[Martinez] Excuse me.

537
00:41:57,556 --> 00:41:59,350
[suspenseful music playing]

538
00:42:10,778 --> 00:42:12,488
[tense music playing]

539
00:42:23,916 --> 00:42:25,626
[Arnaldo] Okay, I would like
to propose a toast

540
00:42:25,709 --> 00:42:28,254
for Ardiente's very special woman.

541
00:42:28,879 --> 00:42:29,964
Ivy Aguas.

542
00:42:30,714 --> 00:42:32,883
For all the help you've given our family.

543
00:42:35,135 --> 00:42:37,346
-Cheers.
-Cheers.

544
00:42:43,769 --> 00:42:47,314
Once again, Miss Aguas,
thank you for your help.

545
00:42:47,940 --> 00:42:50,526
Well, it was my pleasure to extend my help

546
00:42:50,609 --> 00:42:51,944
to the Ardiente family.

547
00:42:52,861 --> 00:42:55,114
If that happened to me,

548
00:42:55,197 --> 00:42:58,200
I wouldn't stop until justice was served.

549
00:42:58,867 --> 00:43:03,831
And until I take back
what's only rightfully mine.

550
00:43:09,003 --> 00:43:10,254
To Ivy Aguas.

551
00:43:11,505 --> 00:43:13,215
For the Ardiente family.

552
00:43:14,341 --> 00:43:16,218
-For the Ardiente family.
-Cheers.

553
00:43:39,617 --> 00:43:40,534
Arnaldo.

554
00:43:41,201 --> 00:43:45,205
I couldn't help but notice
you and Miss Aguas…

555
00:43:45,789 --> 00:43:49,001
are growing closer.

556
00:43:50,669 --> 00:43:53,005
Am I hearing wedding bells?

557
00:43:54,173 --> 00:43:55,215
I'm not going to lie, Grandpa.

558
00:43:55,299 --> 00:43:59,261
Someday, I want that firecracker
to be the mother of my children.

559
00:43:59,345 --> 00:44:01,639
Firecracker? [chuckles]

560
00:44:02,389 --> 00:44:04,808
A fitting description of this woman.

561
00:44:05,851 --> 00:44:07,102
Interesting.

562
00:44:07,186 --> 00:44:09,688
It seems like you're drunk
on love, or should I say…

563
00:44:10,898 --> 00:44:11,774
lust?

564
00:44:12,107 --> 00:44:16,028
That's why you're forgetting
about the whole set-up.

565
00:44:16,111 --> 00:44:17,237
Set-up?

566
00:44:17,946 --> 00:44:21,825
Come on, Arnaldo. Don't be stupid.

567
00:44:22,159 --> 00:44:25,079
Because of your actions, you're
starting to look like a fool.

568
00:44:26,080 --> 00:44:29,416
Or have you forgotten
Miss Aguas' transgressions

569
00:44:29,500 --> 00:44:30,709
against our family?

570
00:44:30,793 --> 00:44:31,794
[scoffs]

571
00:44:33,295 --> 00:44:36,340
All right. What exactly are those?

572
00:44:37,091 --> 00:44:40,511
-So far, all we have are doubts.
-Oh, come on, Arnaldo.

573
00:44:41,011 --> 00:44:44,598
If anything, Grandpa…
We've proven her loyalty.

574
00:44:45,099 --> 00:44:47,726
I don't understand
where your anger is coming from.

575
00:44:48,644 --> 00:44:50,437
Watch your tone, young man--

576
00:44:50,521 --> 00:44:52,940
How about you watch
your priorities, Congressman?

577
00:44:54,983 --> 00:44:58,195
If you focus on this unfounded
suspicion against Ivy…

578
00:44:58,612 --> 00:45:00,948
[scoffs] we're going to have a problem.

579
00:45:18,674 --> 00:45:23,679
[upbeat music playing]

580
00:45:28,225 --> 00:45:29,226
It's hot.

581
00:45:30,185 --> 00:45:33,230
The weather or Miss Ivy Aguas?

582
00:45:34,940 --> 00:45:36,108
Go on, Raul.

583
00:45:36,191 --> 00:45:38,652
Try to say something I wouldn't like.

584
00:45:42,072 --> 00:45:45,617
[Julio] Careful, Raul.
You're being watched by a hawk.

585
00:46:02,384 --> 00:46:05,846
Emilia, the heat's unbearable, huh?

586
00:46:06,221 --> 00:46:07,639
I know, Ivy.

587
00:46:09,183 --> 00:46:12,978
But I have an even hotter scoop.

588
00:46:17,566 --> 00:46:19,485
Is there something between you and my son?

589
00:46:21,111 --> 00:46:23,697
Are you guys officially a couple?

590
00:46:25,199 --> 00:46:27,075
Or is that fake news?

591
00:46:27,618 --> 00:46:30,204
If it's true, what's wrong with that?

592
00:46:30,287 --> 00:46:33,457
I'm single. So is Arnaldo.

593
00:46:33,790 --> 00:46:38,045
If ever that happens,
we would be a hot couple.

594
00:46:38,128 --> 00:46:40,297
We'd be hotter than summer.

595
00:46:40,631 --> 00:46:42,549
You know, I just realized something.

596
00:46:44,218 --> 00:46:47,346
Just when Papa started
to become suspicious of you,

597
00:46:47,429 --> 00:46:51,099
why'd you cling to my son
like a jellyfish?

598
00:46:51,183 --> 00:46:52,309
[chuckles]

599
00:46:52,726 --> 00:46:55,437
Emilia, just a case of perfect timing.

600
00:46:55,854 --> 00:46:56,897
Oh…

601
00:46:56,980 --> 00:46:59,608
Some people have
a different term for it, though.

602
00:47:00,192 --> 00:47:02,069
Perfect manipulation.

603
00:47:02,778 --> 00:47:04,905
Are you calling me a manipulator?

604
00:47:04,988 --> 00:47:06,657
[scoffs] Of course not!

605
00:47:07,991 --> 00:47:12,579
But… you just know how to play
with the good people,

606
00:47:12,663 --> 00:47:14,081
who you can benefit from.

607
00:47:14,164 --> 00:47:17,209
As the saying goes,
"It takes one to know one."

608
00:47:17,292 --> 00:47:18,252
Right?

609
00:47:18,335 --> 00:47:23,882
But I won't allow my son
to be used by someone

610
00:47:23,966 --> 00:47:26,385
who could betray our family.

611
00:47:27,386 --> 00:47:29,680
Wait, I'm not saying
you're a traitor, okay?

612
00:47:30,639 --> 00:47:32,099
It's purely hypothetical.

613
00:47:32,975 --> 00:47:35,477
[dramatic music]

614
00:47:42,067 --> 00:47:43,986
This is also hypothetical, Emilia.

615
00:47:44,069 --> 00:47:48,574
This is hypothetical, okay?
What if I kill you right here?

616
00:47:49,408 --> 00:47:50,450
Hmm?

617
00:47:50,909 --> 00:47:52,411
Here! There you go.

618
00:47:52,494 --> 00:47:54,413
[choking]

619
00:47:54,496 --> 00:47:55,956
Well?

620
00:47:56,748 --> 00:47:59,084
-Emilia!
-Serves you right!

621
00:47:59,167 --> 00:48:00,919
You deserve to die!

622
00:48:01,003 --> 00:48:03,630
-Ivy!
-I'm going to kill you.

623
00:48:03,714 --> 00:48:04,965
-You're going to die.
-Ivy!

624
00:48:05,048 --> 00:48:06,174
-Ivy!
-Stay out of this!

625
00:48:06,258 --> 00:48:07,384
-Stop it!
-Ivy, stop!

626
00:48:07,467 --> 00:48:10,095
-I'm going to kill her!
-Stop it!

627
00:48:10,178 --> 00:48:11,388
-Die, Emilia!
-Ivy!

628
00:48:11,471 --> 00:48:12,931
-Stay out of this!
-Ivy! Ivy! Stop it, Ivy!

629
00:48:13,015 --> 00:48:14,141
-Help me!
-Ivy!

630
00:48:15,892 --> 00:48:17,352
-Ivy!
-Get off me!

631
00:48:17,436 --> 00:48:18,812
[groans]

632
00:48:20,647 --> 00:48:23,942
Ivy, are you okay? You seem agitated.

633
00:48:26,153 --> 00:48:27,863
[chuckles]

634
00:48:31,783 --> 00:48:32,784
Well…

635
00:48:33,785 --> 00:48:35,996
I know where you're coming from, Emilia.

636
00:48:36,079 --> 00:48:40,000
But that's why I helped you
find Governor Alvarez

637
00:48:40,083 --> 00:48:44,129
to prove my loyalty to your family.

638
00:48:46,006 --> 00:48:48,383
As for me and Arnaldo,

639
00:48:49,217 --> 00:48:50,385
we aren't official.

640
00:48:51,261 --> 00:48:53,180
But once that happens,

641
00:48:53,263 --> 00:48:56,642
I'll text you,
so you aren't late to the scoop.

642
00:48:58,268 --> 00:48:59,311
Excuse me.

643
00:49:19,998 --> 00:49:21,375
<i>There's no turning back, Ivy.</i>

644
00:49:21,458 --> 00:49:24,795
<i>I may be far away from you,</i>
<i>but you have my full support.</i>

645
00:49:24,878 --> 00:49:28,799
<i>Who do you think is capable</i>
<i>of leading this town?</i>

646
00:49:28,882 --> 00:49:30,509
<i>Aside from us, the Ardientes?</i>

647
00:49:30,592 --> 00:49:34,304
<i>Me! I will run for governor</i>
<i>against you, Arnaldo!</i>

648
00:49:36,515 --> 00:49:37,974
[Arnaldo] <i>You helped Diego.</i>

649
00:49:38,058 --> 00:49:40,686
[Ivy] <i>May I just remind you, Mr. Mayor,</i>

650
00:49:40,769 --> 00:49:44,648
<i>we aren't together</i>
<i>for you to feel jealous.</i>

651
00:49:44,731 --> 00:49:45,649
<i>Mr. Mayor.</i>

652
00:49:45,732 --> 00:49:46,858
<i>Out of my room!</i>

653
00:49:46,942 --> 00:49:48,151
<i>-Do it again.</i>
<i>-Get out!</i>

654
00:49:48,235 --> 00:49:50,362
<i>No, because I will keep</i>
<i>coming back for more.</i>

655
00:49:51,321 --> 00:49:52,364
<i>Arnaldo!</i>

656
00:49:52,447 --> 00:49:55,951
[theme music playing]
